# Committed content is LF, and a checkout must not silently rewrite it.
#
# The pages under docs/src are generated by scripts/docs-matrix.js and
# scripts/docs-errors.js, and their `--check` mode compares the file on disk with
# a freshly generated one. GitHub's windows-latest runner checks out with
# `core.autocrlf=true` and this repository had no attribute declaring the line
# ending, so those pages arrived as CRLF there, the comparison failed, and CI went
# red on a page whose content was correct (public-docs-site-and-provider-matrix,
# R1-1). The generators now also normalise line endings before comparing, so this
# file is the second half of the fix: it keeps every clone's working tree byte
# identical to the committed content.
#
# Scoped to the generated pages rather than `* text=auto eol=lf`: normalising the
# whole tree would rewrite unrelated files in existing clones for no benefit here.
docs/src/** text eol=lf

# scripts/ is plain Node and is read as text by the same checks.
scripts/** text eol=lf
